out=['# Manuscript structural audit','## Scope and file safety','The entire DOCX body was read before editing: 388 body blocks, including 16 tables, 20 embedded images (19 scientific and one journal example), all captions and Methods. Comments, footnotes, endnotes and footer text were inspected. Footnotes/endnotes contain no substantive study text. Six comments contain editorial/template notes, including caption and section advice and an Abstract concision comment; none supplies missing analysis results. Images were visually inspected; fine labels are frequently not readable enough for numerical verification.','The original manuscript was treated as read-only. Its SHA-256 fingerprint is recorded in `manuscript_work/original_sha256.txt`. New DOCX and Markdown copies were generated independently. No external references, methods defaults, data, models or experimental findings were introduced. This is an internal structural/evidence audit, not raw-data reanalysis or reference authentication.','[AUTHOR CHECK — Confirm target journal: Communications Biology or Nature Communications.]','## CURRENT STRUCTURE','1. B0000–B0013: Nature Communications submission template.\n2. B0014–B0028: study title/authors, Abstract and Introduction with four hypotheses and AI claims.\n3. B0031–B0075: collection/QC, annotation, whole pangenome, rarity, graph and exploratory structure.\n4. B0076–B0118: substantial functional-genomics Results with twelve subsections.\n5. B0121–B0179: whole Heaps, clinical/environmental architecture, shared comparison, four-cluster differential result, clinical Heaps and repeated interpretation.\n6. B0182–B0209: consensus divergence and descriptive geography.\n7. B0212–B0225: IQ-TREE results and detailed accession tables.\n8. B0228–B0240: fluidity results followed by duplicated annotation/architecture.\n9. B0242–B0260: template Results examples and empty template Discussion.\n10. B0262–B0355: uneven Methods—collection/dedup/QC, consensus geography, SNP/phylogeny, fluidity, then FuncScan, with fluidity interpretation stranded after FuncScan.\n11. B0356–B0386: genuine fluidity equation image adjacent to template availability, reference and supplementary instructions; template graphene table.','## MAJOR STRUCTURAL PROBLEMS','The draft has a coherent underlying result—conserved backbone plus extensive accessory heterogeneity—but interleaves procedural history, repeated conclusions, predictions and incomplete translational aims. There is no developed Discussion, no study bibliography, and no reproducible downstream Methods for several strong numerical Results. Source-comparison versions and QC arithmetic conflict. Repeated section and figure numbers make the original hierarchy unreliable.','The new architecture moves from collection → global architecture → accumulation → source variation → functional landscape → clinical fluidity → core phylogeny → descriptive geography. Methods mirror these dependencies; fluidity precedes phylogeny because it uses the presence/absence matrix and does not depend on the alignment. Translation is discussed as implication/future work, not as fabricated Results.','## ANALYSIS INVENTORY','Classification definitions: COMPLETE means an explicit procedure and substantive outcome are documented sufficiently to identify the analysis; software/reporting gaps may remain. PARTIAL means outcome and some procedure exist but material definitions or outputs are missing. RESULTS ONLY means a numerical outcome is stated without a corresponding documented procedure (including Abstract-only counts). METHODS ONLY means a procedure is described but no result is supplied. MENTIONED ONLY means an aim/use/future possibility. NOT SUPPORTED BY MANUSCRIPT means no evidence of that completed analysis, or the draft explicitly says it was not done.','| # | Analysis | Status | Original evidence | Assessment | New location |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
